as formerly known as Penn National Gaming, Inc. and changed its name to PENN Entertainment, Inc. in August 2022. PENN Entertainment, Inc. was founded in 1972 and is based in Wyomissing, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jay A. Snowden | President, CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $5.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 23K people. Revenue per employee of $297K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 17\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["PENN Entertainment, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $2.3B market cap on $7.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $140M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -1.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 15.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 17% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 57/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Cyclical peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"AQR Capital Reports 1.09% Ownership Stake in PENN Entertainment as of September 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/aqr-capital-reports-109-ownership-stake-in-penn-entertainment-as-of-september-2026","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794577138.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"PENN Q3 2026 deep dive: retail and interactive growth offset margin challenges","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/penn-q3-2026-deep-dive-134136700.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794318096.0